From b73b11436f6a80e2a99f494bdde81cc57796dbd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:06:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] v4l2bufferpool: Don't take an empty error buffer for the
 end of stream

An M2M encoder that fails a job returns the CAPTURE buffer with
V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR and bytesused 0: no data was produced. The capture
path of gst_v4l2_buffer_pool_process() treats any empty buffer from an
M2M device as the drain marker of legacy drivers and returns
GST_V4L2_FLOW_LAST_BUFFER. v4l2videoenc then stops its processing loop
and unlocks its OUTPUT queue, the next input frame fails with
GST_FLOW_FLUSHING, upstream pauses, and the pipeline never reaches EOS:

  hantro-vpu (RK3588 VEPU121), one injected encoder fault in a 30 frame
  videotestsrc ! v4l2jpegenc ! multifilesink run:
  - fault on the first frame: stuck in PREROLLING, 0 frames out
  - timeout on a later frame: 16 of 30 frames, then stuck

The driver keeps both queues running and returns the failed buffers
with the error flag, as the stateful encoder interface specifies.

A buffer flagged with an error is no drain marker. Give it back to the
pool and return GST_V4L2_FLOW_CORRUPTED_BUFFER, which the elements
already handle by moving on to the next buffer.

With this and the previous change, the same runs end with EOS and 29 of
30 frames: only the failed frame is missing.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 sys/v4l2/gstv4l2bufferpool.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2bufferpool.c b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2bufferpool.c
index 2b96f2e..787c8e6 100644
--- a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2bufferpool.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2bufferpool.c
@@ -1999,6 +1999,21 @@ gst_v4l2_buffer_pool_process (GstV4l2BufferPool * pool, GstBuffer ** buf,
             guint num_queued;
             gsize size = gst_buffer_get_size (*buf);
 
+            /* A capture buffer returned with V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR carries no
+             * valid data, and it may well be empty, e.g. when an encoder
+             * failed to encode a frame. It is not the empty buffer of a
+             * drained legacy M2M device: drop it, and keep the stream
+             * going. */
+            if (size == 0 && GST_V4L2_IS_M2M (obj->device_caps) &&
+                GST_BUFFER_FLAG_IS_SET (*buf, GST_BUFFER_FLAG_CORRUPTED)) {
+              GST_WARNING_OBJECT (pool,
+                  "Dropping empty buffer flagged with an error");
+              gst_v4l2_buffer_pool_resize_buffer (bpool, *buf);
+              gst_buffer_unref (*buf);
+              *buf = NULL;
+              return GST_V4L2_FLOW_CORRUPTED_BUFFER;
+            }
+
             /* Legacy M2M devices return empty buffer when drained */
             if (size == 0 && GST_V4L2_IS_M2M (obj->device_caps)) {
               gst_v4l2_buffer_pool_resize_buffer (bpool, *buf);
